    "title": "Artemis II flight tracker. Monday updates on Orion location, moon flyby",
    "text": "SPACEArtemis II tracker: Live updates as astronauts start lunar flyby todayCheryl McCloud Eric LagattaUSA TODAY NETWORK - FloridaUpdated April 6, 2026, 11:40 a.m. ETToday, Monday, April 6, is the day for the four astronauts on the Artemis II mission.They'll approach the moon for a lunar flyby, seeing sights never before seen by human eyes, along with spectacular views of the Earth.On Easter Sunday, the crew entered the lunar sphere of influence, where the pull of the moon’s gravity became stronger than the pull of the Earth’s gravity.If you purchase through our links, the USA Today Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
